From 63add596060046e15ee9172c393f1924bc67c803 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 09:59:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] trans: a zero-sized place that is a static or sits behind a pointer
 is borrowed at its real address

py314-ast_serialize 0.13.1 (pyo3 0.29.2, abi3; first consumer py314-mypy 2.4.1): `import ast_serialize` died with
SIGBUS inside the module exec function. gdb: pc and ctr were a stack address (an indirect call through garbage) and
r3, the PyObject* passed to that call, another stack address; the frames above were pyo3's cast-error formatter under
PyErrState::restore under __pyo3_module_exec. In an abi3 build every CPython type object is an opaque zero-sized
extern static (`extern static PyModule_Type: PyTypeObject`, `PyTypeObject { _private: [u8; 0] }`) and pyo3-ffi's
`PyModule_Check` compares `Py_TYPE(op)` with `&raw mut PyModule_Type`. codegen_c's Borrow arm answered `(void*)&rv`
(the address of the return slot) for EVERY zero-sized source, so the comparison failed, the downcast of the module
object raised a cast error, and the formatter asked that stack address for its `__qualname__`.

The shortcut exists because zero-sized locals have no C declaration (disallow_empty_structs). It now applies only to
a place rooted in a local, argument or the return slot and reached without a deref; a static (an extern one has the
symbol's address) or anything behind a pointer goes through emit_borrow, whose Deref and Field paths already handle
zero-sized places, and a plain static becomes `&sym.val`.

Assisted-by: Claude Fable 5.1
---

diff --git a/src/trans/codegen_c.cpp b/src/trans/codegen_c.cpp
index cc36e4b8..b47a051f 100644
--- a/src/trans/codegen_c.cpp
+++ b/src/trans/codegen_c.cpp
@@ -4653,7 +4653,16 @@ namespace {
                 TU_ARMA(Borrow, ve) {
                     emit_lvalue(e.dst);
                     m_of << " = ";
-                    if( this->type_is_bad_zst(m_mir_res->get_lvalue_type(tmp, ve.val, ve.val.m_wrappers.size())) ) {
+                    // A zero-sized place has no storage of its own only when it is (part of) a local, argument or the
+                    // return slot reached without a deref: those aren't declared, so any valid address does. A static
+                    // (an extern one has the symbol's address: pyo3's `&raw mut PyModule_Type`) or anything behind
+                    // a pointer has a real address the program may compare, so emit_borrow computes it.
+                    bool no_storage = !ve.val.m_root.is_Static();
+                    for(const auto& w : ve.val.m_wrappers) {
+                        if( w.is_Deref() )
+                            no_storage = false;
+                    }
+                    if( no_storage && this->type_is_bad_zst(m_mir_res->get_lvalue_type(tmp, ve.val, ve.val.m_wrappers.size())) ) {
                         m_of << "(void*)&rv";
                     }
                     else {
